<title>TURKEY: Turkish central bank buys lira for dollars.</title>
<headline>Turkish central bank buys lira for dollars.</headline>
<dateline>ISTANBUL 1997-07-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Turkish central bank bought lira for dollars to save its currency, bankers said.</p>
<p>They said the bank started to buy lira at around 157,520 to the dollar. The lira firmed to 157,350 levels after the intervention.</p>
<p>The lira had weakened to 157,550 to the dollar in the currency interbank in line with the dollar's strength in the world markets.</p>
</text>
